#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:19
msgid "5. Weather Monitor with ThingSpeak"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:28
msgid "This project collects temperature and pressure data using an Atmospheric Pressure Sensor. The collected data is then transmitted to the ThingSpeak cloud platform through the ESPC2-01 module and the Wi-Fi network at regular time intervals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:32
msgid "1. Build the Circuit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:36
msgid "The module draws a high current at start-up, so make sure the 9 V battery or an external power supply is plugged into the DC jack of the R4 Minima."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:43
msgid ":ref:`cpn_uno`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:44
msgid ":ref:`cpn_espc201`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:45
msgid ":ref:`cpn_bmp280`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:49
msgid "2. Configure ThingSpeak"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:51
msgid "|link_thingspeak| ™ is an IoT analytics platform service that allows you to aggregate, visualize and analyze live data streams in the cloud. ThingSpeak provides instant visualizations of data posted by your devices to ThingSpeak. With the ability to execute MATLAB® code in ThingSpeak you can perform online analysis and processing of the data as it comes in. ThingSpeak is often used for prototyping and proof of concept IoT systems that require analytics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:61
msgid "**2.1 Creating ThingSpeak Account**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:63
msgid "The first thing you need to do is to create an account with ThingSpeak. Since the collaboration with MATLAB, you can use your MathWorks credentials to login to |link_thingspeak|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:65
msgid "If you do not have one, you need to create an account with MathWorks and login to ThingSpeak Application."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:72
msgid "**2.2 Creating the channel**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:74
msgid "After logging in, create a new channel to store the data by going to \"Channels\" > \"My Channels\" and clicking on \"New Channel\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:79
msgid "For this project, we need to create a channel called \"**Weather Monitor**\" with two fields: **Field 1** for \"**Temperature**\" and **Field 2** for \"**Atmospheric Pressure**\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:90
msgid "3. Run the Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:92
msgid "Open the ``05-Weather_monitor.ino`` file under the path of ``ultimate-sensor-kit\\code\\iot_project_espc201\\wifi\\05-Weather_monitor``, or copy this code into **Arduino IDE**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:96
msgid "The sketch needs the **Adafruit BMP280** library. Open the Library Manager, search for ``Adafruit BMP280`` and install it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:100
msgid "Type the name and the password of your own Wi-Fi network."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:107
msgid "Paste the **Write API Key** of your ThingSpeak channel into ``myAPI``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:118
msgid "Use the **Write** key of the channel, not the Read key, and not the User key. Keep it private: anyone with that key can push data into your channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:121
msgid "Select **Arduino UNO R4 Minima** and the right port, then click **Upload**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:123
msgid "Open the Serial Monitor at **115200**. After a few seconds you should read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:132
msgid "and then, every 20 seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:143
msgid "If you read ``Could not find a BMP280, check the wiring and the address``, run the I2C scanner or simply try the other address: some modules answer on ``0x77`` instead of ``0x76``. The sketch already tries both, so this message means neither one answered - check SDA, SCL, VCC and GND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:154
msgid "Open your ThingSpeak channel. A new point appears on the graph every 20 seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:158
msgid "A free ThingSpeak channel accepts one update every 15 seconds. The sketch waits 20, so you never lose a point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:163
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:165
msgid "This project does not use Blynk. The board talks to ThingSpeak with plain HTTP over the AT commands, exactly like a browser asks for a web page - which is why you can watch the values in any browser afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:169
msgid "**What you have to fill in**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:179
msgid "The host and the port never change. Only the API key is personal - it tells ThingSpeak which channel the numbers belong to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:182
msgid "**The serial port that talks to the module**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:184
msgid "The ESPC2-01 works as a modem: the sketch sends it AT commands on D0/D1, which is ``Serial1``, a hardware port, so 115200 works without bit errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:191
msgid "``espModuleInit()`` waits for the module to finish booting and then sends ``ATE0`` to switch the echo off. Without it the boot log and the echoed commands end up mixed into the replies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:195
msgid "**at() - one AT command, with a time limit**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:214
msgid "Every command goes through this one function. It stops as soon as the expected answer arrives, and it **always returns**, so a missing ``OK`` can never freeze the board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:217
msgid "**joinWiFi()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:225
msgid "``AT+CWJAP`` needs several seconds - the module has to find the access point, exchange the keys and get an IP address. That is why it is given 20 seconds while the other commands only need one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:229
msgid "**The BMP280**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:239
msgid "The chip answers on ``0x76`` or ``0x77`` depending on how its SDO pin is wired, so the sketch tries both before it gives up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:242
msgid "**loop() - a timer without delay()**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:250
msgid "``millis()`` counts the milliseconds since power-up. Comparing it with the last update is a delay that does **not** stop the program - the board stays free to do anything else. A free ThingSpeak channel accepts one update every 15 seconds, so 20 seconds is a safe interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:255
msgid "**sendData() - build the request and push it out**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:272
msgid "Three AT commands do the work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:274
msgid "``AT+CIPMUX=0`` - one connection at a time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:275
msgid "``AT+CIPSTART`` - open a TCP connection to ``api.thingspeak.com:80``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:276
msgid "``AT+CIPSEND=<length>`` - the module answers with ``>``, and only then you send the request. The length must be the **exact** number of characters of ``req``, which is why the sketch measures ``req.length()`` instead of guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/wifi_espc201/05-iot_Weather_monitor.rst:280
msgid "``field1`` and ``field2`` are the two columns of your channel. Whatever you name them in ThingSpeak, the numbers land there in that order."
msgstr ""
